# PROLOGUE — "Soundcheck", part 1: the Pink Wyvern before doors.
# Canon: the storyboard doc (v2) and docs/STORY.md. Tone: PG-13, funny first, true second.
# Objectives are derived from flags (src/content/objectives.ts), so chores work in any order.
# Repeat talks never repeat: talk scenes branch on seen.<scene id> (times played before).
# Eddar's voice: Shakespeare's music, Tennyson's longing, Nietzsche's edge. Never pompous, never pathetic.

@scene prologue.intro
# PLOT: Cold open. The Wildfires rehearse for tonight's SAVE THE WORLD heat; Eddar mops; the stranger walks in.
# CHARACTER: Eddar is competent, invisible, and funnier than anyone in the room. Roxy is a rockstar who isn't famous yet.
@bgm wyvern_soundcheck
@card THE PINK WYVERN — SAVE THE WORLD NIGHT
@cam focus roxy
ROXY [smile]: Listen up, Wildfires! Tonight we don't PLAY Save the World. Tonight we ARE the world, and we are SAVING it.
ROXY [smile]: With music to light the heavens! With volume to awaken the dead! With FIRE hot enough to ignite an ocean with!
@emote roxy fire
@sfx cheer
NARRATOR: Scattered applause from the bar. Old Gil claps twice and goes back to his beer.
SPIKE: Save the world? From what...
ROXY [angry]: From being BORING! I'm lead vocals, Spike, not you, so shut F-sharp up!
LULU: Ooh, can we open with the new one? The one with no ending?
ROXY: Not tonight, hon'. Soon, though.
@sfx mop
NARRATOR: Lulu points with her cola. The cola leaves the cup. Eddar's mop is already there.
LULU: You're a saint, Eddar.
EDDAR: No saint, Lulu. Saints are paid in eternity. I'm paid on Fridays, and of the two I'd sooner trust the Friday.
EDDAR: "Save the World," says the poster. As if the world had ever once asked to be saved. It asks only to be mopped.
@sfx door
@flag p.leagues_in
@cmd enter_npc leagues front
@cam focus leagues
NARRATOR: The front door, which is locked, opens. A man walks past the bar without looking at it and sits in the dark corner booth.
NARRATOR: Nobody looks up.
LEDGER: Entry #2,204: Mopped the stage at six. At five past, the band, in their infinite and terrible wisdom, baptised it anew in cola. O tempora, o mores, o Spike.
@flag p.intro
@end

@scene prologue.leagues
# PLOT: The stranger (Leagues Soprano) sits in the corner, says nothing, then "Piss off." Plants his later line "You didn't."
# CHARACTER: Eddar's courtesy and wit under rejection; Leagues' foreboding, rude stillness.
@if seen.prologue.leagues>=3
EDDAR: Some doors are bolted from the inside. I'll not knock thrice on a man.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.leagues>=2
EDDAR: I only meant...
STRANGER: I told you to piss off.
EDDAR: And so you did, twice. A refrain. I'll leave you to your chorus.
LEDGER: Entry #2,205: A man came in through a locked door and told me, twice, to piss off. I have been told so before, but never by anyone whose eyes were lit from within. One wonders what he saw that made him look away.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.leagues>=1
EDDAR: The notes on your robe. Is that a song? It looks like one someone stopped halfway through.
STRANGER: Piss off.
@end
@endif
NARRATOR: A robe the moths have feasted on for a century. Gold notes, faded to the colour of old teeth, crawl across it. Beneath it, a breastplate as black as a closed piano lid.
NARRATOR: His eyes are white, and they are lit.
? "Nice robe. I like it." -> robe
? "Doors aren't open yet, friend." -> doors
? "Can I get you anything?" -> anything
* robe
EDDAR: Nice robe. I like it. Moth-eaten is very in this year.
@goto stare
* doors
EDDAR: Doors aren't open yet, friend. Though I see the door disagreed.
@goto stare
* anything
EDDAR: Can I get you anything? Water? A menu? A reason?
* stare
NARRATOR: He looks at Eddar for a long moment. He says nothing.
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_1
# PLOT: Chore 1/3. CHARACTER: observational wit.
@sfx mop
EDDAR: Cola, lime, and something that glows. Some men drink to forget. Spike drinks to discover new colours.
@flag p.puddle_1
@set puddles += 1
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_2
# PLOT: Chore 2/3. CHARACTER: a little petty, a lot human.
@sfx mop
EDDAR: This one bears the likeness of Rex Valor. I'll take my time.
EDDAR: ...There. Even a puddle may be redeemed.
@flag p.puddle_2
@set puddles += 1
@end

@scene prologue.puddle_3
# PLOT: Chore 3/3. CHARACTER: the band loves him in their careless way.
@sfx mop
EDDAR: Skate wax, drawn through the cola in a perfect spiral. No accident, this. It's a signature.
ROXY [smile]: You're welcome!
@flag p.puddle_3
@set puddles += 1
@end

@scene prologue.roxy
# PLOT: Introduce Roxy's stakes (Velvet Kane, the Grand Stadium, her brothers) and the amp hum.
# CHARACTER: big, theatrical, all-in; the fire is fear in a leather jacket. Eddar's quiet devotion.
@if p.amp_fixed
@if talk.roxy_after>=1
ROXY [smile]: Stop hovering, lucky charm. You'll jinx her. Go be lucky at somebody else.
@end
@endif
ROXY [smile]: Listen to her, Eddar. Clean as a church bell. If we don't win tonight, it won't be the amp's fault. It'll be Spike's.
SPIKE: Fair.
@set talk.roxy_after += 1
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_hum_back
ROXY [angry]: Three bars, Eddar. I got THREE BARS of glory and then BZZZ, like the universe clearing its throat AT me.
EDDAR: Ground loops are like grudges. They hide, and they come back.
ROXY [angry]: Then find it before Velvet Kane walks in and hears my destiny GARGLING.
@emote roxy fire
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_checked
ROXY [angry]: Eddar. Amp. Eddar. AMP. I'm drawing you a MAP with my EYES.
@end
@endif
@cam focus roxy
@sfx amp_buzz
@emote roxy fire
ROXY [angry]: NO. No, no, no, no, NO. Do you HEAR that? That is the sound of my DESTINY being GARGLED by a TOASTER.
EDDAR: A sixty-cycle hum, Roxy. It means no malice. It's only the world, clearing its throat.
ROXY [angry]: Then tell the world to clear it SOMEWHERE ELSE! If we win tonight's heat, we play the Grand Stadium. Ten thousand people, and Velvet Kane with a pen that can change our LIVES.
SPIKE: Hair.
ROXY [angry]: My hair is EXPRESSING ITSELF, Spike!
? "Let me look at it." -> look
? "Your hair is a fire hazard." -> hazard {bond_roxy:-1}
? "What happens if you win?" -> win {bond_roxy:+1}
* win
NARRATOR: Her fire gutters low.
ROXY: If we win, my brothers get shoes that fit before the next growth spurt. Mikey's wearing my old boots, Eddar. They've got flames on them. He's nine.
EDDAR: Then the amp will not hum. I swear it on the boots.
@flag p.mikey_boots
@goto charm
* hazard
EDDAR: Your hair, Roxy, is less a hairstyle than a weather warning.
ROXY [angry]: And your mouth is about to be a CRIME SCENE. Fix. The. Amp.
@goto done
* look
EDDAR: Let me look at it. Two minutes. Perhaps three, if it's shy.
* charm
ROXY [smile]: You're my lucky charm, you know that? Now GO. BE. LUCKY.
* done
@flag p.amp_checked
@end

@scene prologue.amp
# PLOT: Two-stage amp puzzle. The ground lift holds for three bars; the real fix is a punch, with a violet flare nobody sees (T4).
# CHARACTER: competence, then a rare loss of temper; Roxy's forehead kiss.
@if !p.amp_checked
EDDAR: "Property of Roxy Vega. Touch it and die." A fair contract. I'll ask her first.
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_fixed
@if seen.prologue.amp>=3
EDDAR: There's a dent shaped like my knuckles in the casing. Roxy hasn't noticed. Roxy will notice.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Purring now, like a cat that has eaten a smaller, louder cat.
@end
@endif
@if p.amp_hum_back
@goto round_two
@endif
@sfx amp_buzz
EDDAR: The tubes glow like a row of patient saints, and the cables sit true. And yet the hum persists, like a regret.
* first_try
? Flip the ground lift. -> lift {harmony:+1}
? Replace the power tube. -> tube
* tube
@sfx clunk
EDDAR: A new tube. Same hum, two tokens poorer. Wisdom is expensive, and it comes in glass.
@set tokens -= 2
@goto first_try
* lift
@sfx switch
NARRATOR: Click. The hum drops away.
ROXY [smile]: Oh. OH. Okay! Count it in, Lulu!
@sfx guitar_riff
NARRATOR: Roxy tears into the riff. One bar. Two. The neon over the stage brightens. On the third bar...
@sfx amp_buzz
NARRATOR: ...the hum comes back louder, like it went out for reinforcements.
ROXY [angry]: EDDAR!
@emote roxy fire
SPIKE: Hair.
ROXY [angry]: I KNOW ABOUT THE HAIR, SPIKE!
@flag p.amp_hum_back
@end
* round_two
@sfx amp_buzz
EDDAR: The ground was a bandage. The hum comes from within: the transformer, singing to itself.
? Swap the fuse. -> fuse
? Tighten the mounts. -> mounts
* fuse
@sfx clunk
EDDAR: A new fuse. The same song. Fuses never sing; they only die.
@goto temper
* mounts
@sfx clunk
EDDAR: Tight. Tighter. Tightest. Still humming. It isn't loose. It's merely rude.
* temper
EDDAR: Thirty minutes to doors. A woman with a pen. A boy of nine in his sister's burning boots. And you, smug little coil, humming as though none of it matters.
EDDAR: Hear me, then. It matters.
? Hit it. -> punch
? Count to ten. Then hit it. -> punch {harmony:+1}
* punch
@sfx punch
@fx violet eddar
@cam shake
NARRATOR: He punches the transformer. For half a heartbeat the dent glows violet. Then it's just a dent.
NARRATOR: The hum stops like a needle lifted from a record. Nobody sees the light, not even Eddar, who is busy shaking out his hand.
SPIKE: Did you just punch Roxy's amp?
EDDAR: A diagnostic tap.
SPIKE: It worked.
EDDAR: Most diagnostics do, if you mean them.
@flag p.amp_fixed
@unflag p.amp_hum_back
@cam focus roxy
@sfx guitar_riff
ROXY [smile]: Is that... OH. That's CLEAN. Sweet screaming amplifiers, LISTEN to her! C'mere, lucky charm!
@emote roxy kiss
NARRATOR: She kisses his forehead and is back at the mic before he can blink.
LEDGER: Entry #2,206: Forehead. Again. Not the cheek, or the mouth... The brow is a fine and sacred country, I am told; but I should dearly like, one day, to visit the capital.
@end

@scene prologue.trash_call
# PLOT: Both chores done: Mama Dee sends Eddar out back. The stranger looks at someone for the first time.
# CHARACTER: Mama Dee's gravel and honey; Leagues' attention, unexplained.
@cam focus mama_dee
MAMA DEE: Eddar! Trash. Alley. Now, before the doors open and the whole Bay smells my kitchen.
EDDAR: The glamour of it all.
@cam focus leagues
NARRATOR: In the corner booth, the stranger's white eyes follow Eddar to the back door. It is the first time he has looked at anyone.
@flag p.trash_called
@end

@scene prologue.mama_dee
# CHARACTER: Mama Dee — owner, gravel and honey, the only adult who looks out for Eddar. No freeloaders on festival night.
@if p.trash_called
MAMA DEE: Back door, sugar. Trash. And if Rex Valor's out there, you walk past him like he's weather.
EDDAR: Weather doesn't usually put me in a barrel.
MAMA DEE: Then you ain't seen weather in Solace Bay.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.mama_dee>=2
MAMA DEE: I love you like the son I had the good sense not to have. Go do something.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.mama_dee>=1
MAMA DEE: See that one in the corner? Walked in through a locked door and ain't bought so much as a water. Soon as I've got two hands free, he's buying or he's leaving.
@if seen.prologue.leagues>=2
EDDAR: He told me to piss off. Twice, with conviction.
MAMA DEE: Then he's got manners and no money. Worst kind.
@endif
@end
@endif
MAMA DEE: Festival night, sugar. Every bar in the Bay's running a heat, and every fool in the Bay thinks he can sing. You keep that floor dry, and I'll keep the fools paying.
EDDAR: "Save the World," say the posters. A bold claim for a contest judged by applause.
MAMA DEE: Honey, the world don't need saving. It needs a cover charge.
@end

@scene prologue.spike
# CHARACTER: Spike — bass; deadpan; secretly fond of Eddar.
@if p.amp_fixed
@if talk.spike_after>=1
SPIKE: Still not telling her. My silence is a gift. Gifts can be withdrawn.
@end
@endif
SPIKE: I didn't tell her you punched the amp. I want that on the record. I'm holding it over you for life.
@set talk.spike_after += 1
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.spike>=2
SPIKE: Three visits. We're basically married. I get the jukebox in the divorce.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.spike>=1
SPIKE: If we win, Roxy wants a tour. If we lose, Roxy wants revenge. Either way, I'm carrying an amp up some stairs.
@end
@endif
SPIKE: Bass player life. Nobody hears you, but everybody notices when you stop.
EDDAR: Like a heartbeat.
SPIKE: ...I was gonna say plumbing. But sure. Heartbeat.
@end

@scene prologue.lulu
# CHARACTER: Lulu — drums; sunny chaos. PLOT: the festival was once real; plants the song with a missing line.
@if seen.prologue.lulu>=2
LULU: If anybody ever picks a drummer for anything, I'm going to cry.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.lulu>=1
LULU: Gran had a song about it. One verse is short, like somebody cut a line out.
EDDAR: A song with a wound in it. Those are the ones that last.
LULU: Drummers hate a missing beat. You can feel it in your teeth.
@end
@endif
LULU: Did you know Save the World used to be a real thing? Like, old-old. My gran said they used to pick a champion, and everybody sang till sunrise.
EDDAR: Every festival is a funeral for something we've forgotten.
LULU: ...That's so sad. Do you want a gummy?
@end

@scene prologue.gil
# CHARACTER: barfly with micro-stories. PLOT: plants the masked woman's arrival in town, and Leagues' kind.
@if seen.prologue.gil>=2
GIL: I've told you all I know. At my age, that's mostly the names of horses that lost.
@end
@endif
@if seen.prologue.gil>=1
GIL: That fella in the corner. I've seen his kind once before, forty years back, on a pier in the fog. He played a horn until the fog cleared, then walked into the sea.
GIL: Didn't drown. He just... left.
@end
@endif
GIL: Saw a woman ride in this afternoon. Black light-cycle, a black mask, silver hair right down her back. Looked at every face on the boardwalk like she was reading a list.
EDDAR: And did she find the name she sought?
GIL: Kid, everybody's looking for someone. Most of us are just looking for the bathroom.
@end

@scene prologue.jukebox
# PLOT: The living soundtrack: pick the room's song. CHARACTER: Rex's ego (Valor Forever), Eddar's quiet skill.
@if seen.prologue.jukebox>=1
EDDAR: Rex has queued "Valor Forever (Demo)" four times. Rex has recorded a demo.
@else
EDDAR: Every record in here is older than I am, except the one I fixed. I won't say which. It knows.
@endif
? "Neon Heart" -> neon
? "Halcyon Days" -> halcyon
? "Dockside Shuffle" -> dockside
? "Burn Slow" (the Wildfires' demo) -> burn
? "Valor Forever (Demo)" -> valor
? Leave it. -> leave
* neon
@bgm juke_neon_heart
EDDAR: A love song for people who've never been loved back. The Bay's favourite.
@end
* halcyon
@bgm juke_halcyon
EDDAR: Scratched on the chorus. I could fix it. I won't. Some songs should keep their scars.
@end
* dockside
@bgm juke_dockside
EDDAR: Written for dockworkers, by a man who'd never lifted anything heavier than a grudge.
@end
* burn
@bgm juke_burn_slow
ROXY [smile]: Eddar, you ANGEL.
@end
* valor
@bgm juke_valor
SPIKE: Oh no.
LULU: Oh NO.
GIL: Turn it off, kid. I'm begging you.
EDDAR: Art, Nietzsche said, is what keeps us from dying of the truth. He never heard this one.
@end
* leave
@end

@scene prologue.front_door
# PLOT: Explains why the front is locked; points at the real exit. After the Bellshell: the Main Drag is the next build.
@if p.bellshell_done
EDDAR: Out there, the Main Drag, and the whole Bay running down it. I can hear the Static Hounds from here. (The Main Drag opens in the next build.)
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Locked until doors. Mama Dee's rule: nobody in till the floor's clean, and nobody out till the trash is.
EDDAR: The trash goes out the back. Stage right, under the pink EXIT sign.
@end

@scene prologue.back_door_locked
# PLOT: Gate the alley until both chores are done; say which one is missing.
@if p.amp_fixed
MAMA DEE: Floor first, sugar! I can hear your shoes sticking from here!
@end
@endif
@if puddles>=3
EDDAR: The alley can wait. Roxy's amp can't. Soundcheck first, says the woman who signs my paychecks.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: The alley can wait. Floor first, then the amp, says the woman who signs my paychecks.
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- discoverables

@scene prologue.poster_save
# PLOT: The festival, and that it's older than anyone thinks.
@if seen.prologue.poster_save>=1
EDDAR: The small print: "Est. time immemorial. No refunds." Even eternity has a returns policy.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: SAVE THE WORLD. A cartoon guitarist punching a meteor. "Heats tonight in every club. Final at the Grand Stadium."
@end

@scene prologue.poster_rex
# PLOT: Rex's legend before we meet him; the crown to come.
@if seen.prologue.poster_rex>=1
EDDAR: The crown is in gold pen. Rex drew it himself. Prophecy, it seems, is a do-it-yourself affair.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: "REX VALOR: UNDEFEATED." Someone has drawn a crown on him.
@end

@scene prologue.chalkboard
# PLOT: Stakes, and a running gag (Gary) for the Main Drag.
@if seen.prologue.chalkboard>=1
EDDAR: Underneath, smaller: "Who is Gary?" Underneath that, smaller still: "Nobody knows who Gary is."
@end
@endif
EDDAR: "TONIGHT: SAVE THE WORLD HEAT. Roxy and the Wildfires versus the Velvet Undertow versus Gary."
@end

@scene prologue.window
# PLOT: The city outside, festive and unaware.
@if seen.prologue.window>=1
EDDAR: A thousand people out there, singing a song whose words they've forgotten. I envy them, a little.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: The boardwalk is all red streamers and paper meteors. Somebody's selling Canticle cocktails: half rum, half prophecy.
@end

@scene prologue.window_broken
# CHARACTER: Eddar's eye for the beauty in wreckage.
@if seen.prologue.window_broken>=1
EDDAR: Mama Dee will want the glass swept. I'd sweep it now, but the glass is the least broken thing in Solace Bay tonight.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Glass across four tables, and one perfect crab-shaped hole. Somewhere out there, a glazier is about to have the best night of his life.
@end

@scene prologue.spare_guitar
# PLOT: Plants Leagues' guitar.
@if seen.prologue.spare_guitar>=1
EDDAR: There's one gold thread caught in the tuning pegs. I don't remember putting it there.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: The spare guitar on the wall. "Decorative," says Mama Dee. Nobody has ever played it. Dust on every string.
@end

@scene prologue.lost_found
# PLOT: The Cyrano letters, before the alley reveals them. Choice: keep it (Lyra pays it off in Act III).
@if p.letter_kept
EDDAR: The box is lighter by one heart. Mine.
@end
@endif
@if p.letter_returned
EDDAR: One glove, three picks, and my own heart, signed by another man. Still there.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: One glove. Three picks. And a love letter in my own handwriting, signed "Rex."
EDDAR: "Your eyes are two lanterns on a dark sea." I wrote that in March. He must have dropped it on the way to the post.
? Put it back. -> back
? Keep it. -> keep
* back
EDDAR: Some mail shouldn't be returned to sender.
@flag p.letter_returned
@end
* keep
EDDAR: Into my pocket, then. It's in better company.
@flag p.letter_kept
@give rex_letter 1
@end

@scene prologue.tip_jar
# CHARACTER: Mama Dee's warmth; the band's tiny fame.
@if seen.prologue.tip_jar>=1
EDDAR: Mama Dee had a hundred of these buttons made. Ninety-nine remain.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Four tokens and a button: "I SURVIVED THE WILDFIRES."
@end

@scene prologue.amp_manual
# CHARACTER: his competence and his ache.
@if seen.prologue.amp_manual>=1
EDDAR: A note in the margin, in my hand: "Ground loops hide. So do I." I don't remember writing it. I remember meaning it.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: The amp manual, dog-eared and annotated. I read amp manuals for fun. Pity me if you must, but do it quietly.
@end

@scene prologue.set_list
# PLOT: Sets up Leagues' song ("Burn Forever" needs two leads); plants Thunderhorn's ballad ("One Word?").
@if seen.prologue.set_list>=1
EDDAR: Crossed out at the bottom: "One Word?" She never told me what the word was.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: "Burn Slow. Burn Medium. Burn Fast. Burn Forever (??? needs 2 leads)." The question marks are underlined three times.
@end
